From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] the signing keys are an input to plat_mac_permissions.xml

Changing the release keys and rebuilding produces a system in which nothing
with uid 1000 can start. On V83, with every system application signed by the
new platform key:

    E/SELinux: seapp_context_lookup: No match for app with uid 1000,
               seinfo default, name com.android.settings
    E/Zygote : selinux_android_setcontext(1000, 0,
               "default:privapp:targetSdkVersion=27:complete", ...) failed
    F/zygote : JNI FatalError called: ... selinux_android_setcontext failed

and zygote aborts, over and over: SystemUI, Settings, CryptKeeper, anything
that runs as system. The reason is that `plat_mac_permissions.xml` in the
image still carried the **previous** platform certificate -- byte for byte the
file V82 shipped, whose signer decodes to `O=KDAndroid, OU=platform` while the
key that actually signed the applications is `O=Readom, OU=platform`. No
application matches that signer, every one of them gets `seinfo=default`, and
`seapp_contexts` has no rule pairing uid 1000 with `default`, so the lookup
fails and the fork is aborted.

The file is generated by insertkeys.py from keys.conf and the certificates,
and the certificates are meant to be prerequisites of it:

    all_plat_keys := platform media shared testkey
    all_plat_keys := $(all_keys:%=$(dir $(DEFAULT_SYSTEM_DEV_CERTIFICATE))/%.x509.pem)

The second line substitutes over `all_keys`, which this file never defines --
the plat/nonplat split in O renamed the list and left the substitution behind.
`all_plat_keys` therefore expands to nothing, the prerequisite list on the next
rule is empty, and a change that is only in the certificates leaves make with
nothing to notice. `installclean` does not help either: it clears the staged
system directory, not `obj/ETC/plat_mac_permissions.xml_intermediates`, where
the file from 2026-10-23 20:30 sat through the key change of 2026-10-24 and
into V83.

Naming the right variable makes the four certificates prerequisites again, so
the file is rebuilt the moment any of them changes. Nothing else about the rule
moves.

--- a/Android.mk
+++ b/Android.mk
@@ -1095,7 +1095,7 @@
 
 # Should be synced with keys.conf.
 all_plat_keys := platform media shared testkey
-all_plat_keys := $(all_keys:%=$(dir $(DEFAULT_SYSTEM_DEV_CERTIFICATE))/%.x509.pem)
+all_plat_keys := $(all_plat_keys:%=$(dir $(DEFAULT_SYSTEM_DEV_CERTIFICATE))/%.x509.pem)
 
 $(LOCAL_BUILT_MODULE): PRIVATE_MAC_PERMS_FILES := $(all_plat_mac_perms_files)
 $(LOCAL_BUILT_MODULE): $(plat_mac_perms_keys.tmp) $(HOST_OUT_EXECUTABLES)/insertkeys.py \
